Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

DefaultExit [SimTalk]
Sets the Default Exit of the Converter designated by <Path>.
Remarks
The Default Exit applies to the Strategies > Default Exit, MU Attribute, and MU Name.
The figures below illustrate the sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into
your simulation model. The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the MU exits.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.DefaultExit:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
• 1 stands for laterally to the right in the insertion direction
• 2 stands for against the insertion direction
• 3 stands for laterally to the left in the insertion direction
• 0 stands for along the insertion direction
DefaultExit [SimTalk]
