ExitForMU [SimTalk]
Sets the side at which the next entering MU or the MU positioned at the converting point wants to exit the
Converter designated by <Path>.
Remarks
You can only set the attribute ExitForMU in the Strategy method/StrategyCtrl.
Note
The MU cannot exit the Converter at the side at which it entered.
The figures below illustrate the sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into
your simulation model. The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the MU exits.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.ExitForMU:integer
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type integer.
Examples
param entranceNo: integer
if @.name = "C" 
   ?.ExitForMU := 0 /* number of the exit of the converter*/
elseif @.name = "A" 
   if entranceNo = 2 
       ?.ExitForMU := 3
ExitForMU [SimTalk]
