Strategy [SimTalk] - Converter
Sets the Strategy of the Converter designated by <Path>.
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.Strategy:string
Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type string.
You can specify:
• "Default Exit" to make all MUs exit through the Default Exit which you select to the successor
attached to that exit.
• "Straight" to convey the MU straight through to the next station.
• "Feed in" to allow MUs from a branch line to only enter the main line when no part is located on
the main line within the Free Space which you enter. The Free Space is the distance between two
successive MUs on the main line.
• "MU Attribute" to move the MU on according to a built-in or a user-defined attribute of the MU. You
can set the attributes with the method setAttributeList. You can set the default exit with the attribute
DefaultExit.
Strategy [SimTalk] - Converter
Plant Simulation Help 11-2311
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

• "MU Name" to move the MU on according to its name. You can set the default exit with the attribute
DefaultExit. You can set the attributes with the method setAttributeList.
The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the MU exits. The figures below illustrate the
sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into your simulation model.
• "Method" to convey the MU according to the attribute ExitForMU you enter into the Strategy Method
in which you determine the side of the Converter at which the MU will exit the Converter. You can set
the control with the attribute StrategyCtrl.
• "Method at Converting Point" to only determine the target at the converting point with the
attribute ExitForMU, not already before the MU enters the Converter. This strategy is only available for a
Capacity of 1.
The MU always stops at the converting point. Then, Plant Simulation calls the method for determining
the target. In the method you can, for example use ?.ExitForMU := 1. You can set the control with
the attribute StrategyCtrl.
Note
As the Strategy Method is used for determining the side of the exit, the Strategy Method will not be
called when the MU has a route and Automatic Routing is activated.
Example
MyConverter.Strategy := "Straight"
Strategy [SimTalk] - Converter
