StrategyCtrl [SimTalk] - Converter
Designates a Method object of the object designated by <Path>.
Remarks
Type in the source code that determines the side of the Converter designated by <Path> at which the MU
will exit the Converter.
The figures below illustrate the sides depending on the direction in which you inserted the Converter into
your simulation model. The numbers designate the side of the Converter at which the part exits.
Plant Simulation calls the Strategy Method as soon as the MU wants to enter the Converter for the setting
Strategy > Method.
Plant Simulation calls the Strategy Method when the MU has reached the converting point for the setting
Strategy > Method at Converting Point.
You have to set the side with the attribute ExitForMU.
As the Strategy Method is used for determining the side of the exit, the Strategy Method will not be
called when the MU has a route and Automatic Routing is activated.
The default strategy method looks like this:
param entranceNo: integer
?.ExitForMU := 0 /* number of exit */
Type
Attribute
Syntax
<Path>.StrategyCtrl:method
StrategyCtrl [SimTalk] - Converter
11-2314 Plant Simulation Help
Unpublished work. © 2026 Siemens

Assignment Value
You can assign a value of data type method.
Examples
param entranceNo: integer
if @.name = "C" 
    ?.ExitForMU := 0 /* number of the exit of the converter*/
elseif @.name = "A" 
    if entranceNo = 2 
        ?.ExitForMU := 3
    else
        ?.ExitForMU := 0
    end
else
    if entranceNo = 2 
        ?.ExitForMU := 1
    else
        ?.ExitForMU := 0
    end
end
MyConverter.StrategyCtrl := &myStrategyCtrl
SimTalk
ExitForMU [SimTalk]
See also
Strategy Method [Converter]
Automatic Routing [Part, Container]
StrategyCtrl [SimTalk] - Converter
